<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.246 percent from 10.248 percent at the previous auction on October 17.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 23, 1997 (Jan 16, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.246 percent (10.248)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 984.525 million (659.150 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.161 billion (721.150 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.276 percent (10.002-10.293)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.348 percent (10.002-10.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 138 (158)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 159 (163)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
